    <relatedmaterial id="aspace_900084c22a9c9d39f7440fdcc5bad58d">
      <head>Related Materials</head>
      <p>Related collections include the organizational records of Save the Pine Bush, Inc. (apap125), the Louis Ismay papers (ua902-064), the Environmental Studies Program records (ua696-003), the Concerned Citizens Against Crossgates records (apap057), and the Crossgates Regional Shopping Mall collection (apap067). See the subject guide on Conservation and the Environment for further collections relating to environmentalism in the Capital Region and beyond.</p>
    </relatedmaterial>
    <scopecontent id="aspace_e556ea55ac684db9d29f0d1aacc11e50">
      <head>Scope and Contents</head>
      <p>The collection documents Wolcott's involvement with the Pinxter Committee of Albany and Save the Pine Bush, Inc., as well as his general work in historical research, archaeology, and environmental preservation within the Capital Region. </p>
      <p>Materials relating to the planning and advertising of Pinxter Festivals include festival posters and flyers, programs of similar festivals, news clippings, handwritten notes, contact information for craft vendors, correspondence, research material on historic Pinxter festivals and Albany's relevant laws and policies, an early souvenir Tulip Fest envelope, and a small collection of colonial Dutch recipes. Materials relating to the Pine Bush in general and Save the Pine Bush, Inc. in particular include maps, trail guides, event posters and flyers, archaeological reports, research material, news clippings, and meeting notes.</p>
    </scopecontent>
